&lt;p&gt;commit 1cc4608c3ada6ed65b8de2ab1d1b5d08a62120d7&lt;br/&gt;
Author: ptupitsyn &amp;lt;ptupitsyn@gridgain.com&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Date:   2015-10-15T16:07:37Z&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-1696&quot; title=&quot;.Net: Ignite does not start with IBM JDK&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-1696&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-1696&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; .Net: Ignite does not start with IBM JDK&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;hr /&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14959147" author="ptupitsyn" created="Thu, 15 Oct 2015 16:14:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I&apos;ve replaced exact path probing with directory search to simplify code and support both JDKs.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14964842" author="vozerov" created="Tue, 20 Oct 2015 09:18:03 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Honestly, I do not like idea of directory search for two reasons:&lt;br/&gt;
1) Vendors might choose to ship both x86 and x64 DLLs in the same archive;&lt;br/&gt;
2) JAVA_HOME directory structure could contain looots of files. E.g. user could unpack &quot;src.zip&quot; (which is shipped with Java distributive) and significantly increase amount of files/folders inside JAVA_HOME. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our app should be tolerant to such problems. For this reason it is better to have a dictionary of well-known locations and scan them one by one. There are not so many JVM vendors to implement this. Finally, we always have a workaround - ask user to set direct path to DLL.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14964986" author="ptupitsyn" created="Tue, 20 Oct 2015 11:22:18 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Fixed&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15010613" author="githubbot" created="Wed, 18 Nov 2015 09:40:32 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user ptupitsyn closed the pull request at:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/161&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/161&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
